---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/data';
---

<Base title="Privacy and house rules" description="What we store when you vote, comment or sign up, and the rules for the discussion.">
  <article class="wrap prose-page">
    <span class="eyebrow">Plain English</span>
    <h1 class="display">Privacy and house rules</h1>

    <h2>What we store</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>When you vote without an account:</b> your answer, the club you picked, a random ID kept in a cookie on your device, and a scrambled (hashed) version of your IP address used only to stop spam.</li>
      <li><b>When you sign up:</b> your email address, username, club, flair, whether you want our emails, and your password stored as a salted hash we can't read.</li>
      <li><b>When you comment:</b> the comment, the time, and your username, club and flair shown next to it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we use it for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Running your account and showing how each fanbase voted. Totals are shown as percentages; individual votes are never published.</li>
      <li>Emailing you about your account, for example a password reset.</li>
      <li>Emailing you about new hubs and features <b>only if you ticked the box</b>. You can untick it on your <a href={href('/account/')}>account page</a> at any time.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't sell your data or share your email with anyone.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>Two cookies, both needed for the site to work: one remembers your device's votes, the other keeps you logged in. No advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

    <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
    <p>
      Delete it yourself from your <a href={href('/account/')}>account page</a>. Your email, password and profile are erased for good. Your
      votes stay in the totals without anything linking them to you, and your comments stay but show as [deleted].
    </p>

    <h2 id="rules">House rules</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Argue about the decision, not the person.</b> Saying a call was wrong is fine. Saying a referee is corrupt, bent or paid off is not allowed.</li>
      <li><b>No abuse.</b> No slurs, no racism, no threats, no wishing harm on anyone.</li>
      <li><b>No links or spam.</b></li>
      <li><b>One account each.</b> Club changes are limited to once a week so each fanbase's numbers stay honest.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Some of this is blocked automatically. Anyone can report a comment; reported comments are hidden until we review them, and we remove accounts that keep breaking the rules.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    max-width: 760px;
    padding-block: 48px 20px;
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 10px 0 24px;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 56px);
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 32px 0 10px;
    font-size: 21px;
    scroll-margin-top: 100px;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  li,
  p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  b {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
